<header class="start-masthead"><p class="eyebrow">Lab runtime · proposed documentation</p><h1>Develop and maintain the runtime documentation</h1><p>Keep implementation, evidence and the rendered edition synchronized without rewriting history.</p><p class="source-note">Draft prepared on 2026-10-14. Integration and final T21 qualification remain pending.</p></header>

<section id="runtime-maintenance-maintain-one-narrative-source" aria-labelledby="runtime-maintenance-maintain-one-narrative-source-title"><h2 id="runtime-maintenance-maintain-one-narrative-source-title">Maintain one narrative source</h2>

<p>This owned preparation uses narrative.json as the editable prose and source-map.json as its exact public evidence selection. A standard-library generator supplies HTML fragments, shared-shell preview pages and a Markdown mirror from those same section bodies.</p>

<p>The proposed maintained destination is website/source/governance-lab-series/runtime; the shared article renderer supplies the existing documentation shell. Imported docs/lab/runtime pages remain a projection. Directly maintained indexes link to them. Do not edit generated HTML/Markdown as competing prose sources.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-maintenance-follow-the-actual-pipeline" aria-labelledby="runtime-maintenance-follow-the-actual-pipeline-title"><h2 id="runtime-maintenance-follow-the-actual-pipeline-title">Follow the actual pipeline</h2>

<p>The <a href="research/sources/website/build.py">website builder</a> stages maintained sources, renders examples/essays/reference/articles, applies presentation and approved editorial wording, finishes the site, generates final search, runs checks and packages the closure. It does not silently refresh source capture or import Markdown.</p>

<p>The <a href="research/sources/tooling/docs/import_site_docs.py">stdlib importer</a> selects explicit source HTML/article/anchor routes, rewrites links, copies permitted assets and writes an import manifest. Root must add the14 explicit runtime routes, actual source-note packaging and navigation/search judgments. The <a href="research/sources/website/source/governance-lab-series/SITE-MAINTENANCE.md">site instructions</a> and <a href="research/sources/docs/lab/MAINTENANCE.md">Markdown maintenance</a> retain that ownership.</p>

<p>The proposed fragments have section IDs/h2 headings and the start-content/start-masthead/source-notes conventions. Preview uses the existing local assets and canonical concept destinations; it is not a separately published website.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-maintenance-review-source-and-behavior-together" aria-labelledby="runtime-maintenance-review-source-and-behavior-together-title"><h2 id="runtime-maintenance-review-source-and-behavior-together-title">Review source and behavior together</h2>

<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Changed input</th><th scope="col">Required review</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CLI argument/default</td><td>Exact parser/README/profile selection and isolated example</td></tr><tr><td>API schema/resource/remapping</td><td>Actual registry precedence and contract/source fields</td></tr><tr><td>Source/reader/mapper/Context implementation</td><td>True origin/period/history/role/full byte closure</td></tr><tr><td>Authentication/expiry/idempotency</td><td>Current channel, exact key/fingerprint, refusal/recovery</td></tr><tr><td>Installation/publisher</td><td>Owned paths/preimages/receipts/uncertainty and meaningful replay</td></tr><tr><td>Evidence/status</td><td>Exact dated receipt, actual terminal/cleanup and claim ceiling</td></tr><tr><td>Narrative/navigation</td><td>Same-source HTML/Markdown, links/fragments/portability/editorial/search</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

<p>Frozen implementation notices, unsuccessful attempts and historical receipts remain byte-preserved. A prose update does not supply a new admission, source epoch or runtime qualification.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-maintenance-do-not-hide-the-current-composition-gap" aria-labelledby="runtime-maintenance-do-not-hide-the-current-composition-gap-title"><h2 id="runtime-maintenance-do-not-hide-the-current-composition-gap-title">Do not hide the current composition gap</h2>

<p>Family4&#x27;s code exists and its partial Source diagnostic remains preserved, but it is ineligible for final runtime. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T02/family4-dependency-cycle-review-0001.json">causal review</a> shows six inherited preparation-only API inputs in its current role table. Final publication would change the manifest and four selector leaves; current_machine_context_scope is byte-preserved, but that does not remove the cycle.</p>

<p>A reviewed immutable successor must conserve all349 original declarations, select exact historical snapshot technical bindings for those preparation inputs, preserve all original Source/history/signature/guard/period checks and prove closure before another Source build. The <a href="research/sources/docs/plans/0011-lab-runtime-completion/runs/0001-execution/T07/api17-task-local-capture-0004/independent-review-0001.json">capture review</a> preserves its passing preparation checks without suppressing the blocker.</p>

</section>

<section id="runtime-maintenance-acceptance-still-required" aria-labelledby="runtime-maintenance-acceptance-still-required-title"><h2 id="runtime-maintenance-acceptance-still-required-title">Acceptance still required</h2>

<p>This generator can check14 names, five diagram/text equivalents, exact public evidence hashes, command grammar, body identity and owned local links. It cannot prove user comprehension, fresh installation, effectful Work, Session disposal, integrated full34 behavior or empirical margin.</p>

<p>T21 completion still depends on T15/current qualification, final setup/recovery walkthroughs, actual website/editorial/render/search/import integration, final link/body-preservation checks and review of the exact resulting edition. No shared renderer/build/importer, website/dist, live service or private state is changed by this preparation.</p>

</section>

